# Vercel builds only web/ (Project Root Directory = "web"). Exclude the Python
# backend and heavy non-frontend assets so `vercel` uploads stay small.
#
# EVERY PATTERN HERE MUST BE ANCHORED WITH A LEADING "/".
# Unanchored patterns match at EVERY level, not just the repo root. On 2026-07-26 a
# bare `app/` here silently excluded `web/app/` — the whole Next.js App Router — so
# `next build` produced a Pages-Router build containing only /404, and every route on
# production 404'd. The deployment still reported "Ready", because compiling nothing
# succeeds. Anchor the pattern, or you delete the app.
#
# Before promoting any build, check its route table:
#   vercel inspect <deployment-url> --logs
# It must list "Route (app)" with /shop, /cart, /checkout — not a lone /404.
/app/
/alembic/
/alembic.ini
/presentations/
/graphify-out/
/peaceway-online-pharmacy-website/
/design-system/
/docs/
/tasks/
/scripts/
/tests/
/requirements.txt
/pyproject.toml
/runtime.txt
/nixpacks.toml
/railway.json
/Procfile
/.codex/
/package.json
/package-lock.json
/node_modules
*.egg-info/
